     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times a day is 6400 mg/day. The maximum for inpatients is generally 3200 mg/day, so this is twice that.\n- **Risks at this level:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't remove these risks.\n\nMedication orders also need to come from a licensed prescriber, and you've said you're not a clinician. If this is for a real patient, the treating prescriber should enter or confirm it.\n\nIf the intent was a high-dose anti-inflammatory regimen, a typical maximum is **800 mg by mouth three to four times daily**, which is 2400\u20133200 mg/day. It should be taken with food. I can enter that once a prescriber confirms the dose and indication. If 1600 mg was a typo, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
